# Line-ending policy.
#
# The golden-C snapshots are byte-compared against compiler output by
# tests/golden/run_golden_tests.sh. On a Windows checkout git would otherwise
# convert them to CRLF, making all 30 snapshots "differ" from LF-normalized
# generated C on line endings alone - byte-identical content, whole-file diff.
# That failed the first CI run that gated this suite on windows-latest.
#
# The runner now strips CR from both sides regardless, so this file is
# defence in depth: it keeps the working copy honest so a developer on Windows
# sees the same bytes CI does.
*.c.golden text eol=lf

# Shell scripts must keep LF or they break when executed under a Unix shell
# (git-bash on the Windows runner included: a CRLF shebang line yields
# "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M").
*.sh text eol=lf

# Wyn sources: keep LF so `// EXPECT:` comparisons and error-message snapshots
# are stable across platforms.
*.wyn text eol=lf
